      ],
      "image": "assets/images/15401/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine ground beef, onion, and bell pepper in a large saucepan over medium-high heat. Cook and stir until beef is browned, about 5 minutes. Drain excess fat.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/sjf-hCG6uJ1jI_nNqERNK2DKIdY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-15401-Easy-Chili-ddmfs-step-2-bf6967cf4c9547d18d6300a0ffbafe88.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/15401/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Season with chili powder, garlic, cumin, and bay leaf.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/dOegBX9GUvdzrFo70eoX9Y3rVFU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-15401-Easy-Chili-ddmfs-step-4-92bc27c8f6164e198448e023ebe21564.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/15401/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir in tomatoes, tomato sauce, and jalapeños. Bring to a boil and reduce heat to low. Cover and simmer, stirring occasionally, for 1 1/2 hours. Stir in beans and allow to heat through.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
